{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b0602b6a76cc3f84","name":"card_event_molotov_cocktail_fin","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Finland/events/card_event_molotov_cocktail_fin","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"MOLOTOV COCKTAIL","text":"Deal 2 damage. The enemy discards a card. Discard at the end of your turn.","flavorText":"During the Winter War between Finland and the Soviet Union in 1939-1940, Molotov cocktails played a significant role in Finland's defense against the larger and better-equipped Soviet forces. These makeshift incendiary weapons, essentially glass bottles filled with flammable liquid and a cloth wick, were named by the Finns as a mocking reference to Soviet Foreign Minister Vyacheslav Molotov. Finnish soldiers used Molotov cocktails effectively to disrupt and destroy Soviet tanks and vehicles, earning a reputation for tenacity in the face of overwhelming odds. Note that not all Molotov cocktails were improvised in the field. During the Winter War, they were mass-produced by the Alko corporation at a distillery in southern Finland, 45 km from Helsinki, where the bottled mixture of ethanol, tar and gasoline was bundled with matches. The production totalled 450,000 Molotov Cocktails throughout the war.","faction":"Finland","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_molotov_cocktail_fin","title":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_molotov_cocktail_fin_title","SourceString":"MOLOTOV COCKTAIL","LocalizedString":"MOLOTOV COCKTAIL"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Finland","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_molotov_cocktail_fin_text","SourceString":"Deal 2 damage. The enemy discards a card. Discard at the end of your turn.","LocalizedString":"Deal 2 damage. The enemy discards a card. Discard at the end of your turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_finland","Key":"card_event_molotov_cocktail_fin_history","SourceString":"During the Winter War between Finland and the Soviet Union in 1939-1940, Molotov cocktails played a significant role in Finland's defense against the larger and better-equipped Soviet forces. These makeshift incendiary weapons, essentially glass bottles filled with flammable liquid and a cloth wick, were named by the Finns as a mocking reference to Soviet Foreign Minister Vyacheslav Molotov. Finnish soldiers used Molotov cocktails effectively to disrupt and destroy Soviet tanks and vehicles, earning a reputation for tenacity in the face of overwhelming odds. Note that not all Molotov cocktails were improvised in the field. During the Winter War, they were mass-produced by the Alko corporation at a distillery in southern Finland, 45 km from Helsinki, where the bottled mixture of ethanol, tar and gasoline was bundled with matches. The production totalled 450,000 Molotov Cocktails throughout the war.","LocalizedString":"During the Winter War between Finland and the Soviet Union in 1939-1940, Molotov cocktails played a significant role in Finland's defense against the larger and better-equipped Soviet forces. These makeshift incendiary weapons, essentially glass bottles filled with flammable liquid and a cloth wick, were named by the Finns as a mocking reference to Soviet Foreign Minister Vyacheslav Molotov. Finnish soldiers used Molotov cocktails effectively to disrupt and destroy Soviet tanks and vehicles, earning a reputation for tenacity in the face of overwhelming odds. Note that not all Molotov cocktails were improvised in the field. During the Winter War, they were mass-produced by the Alko corporation at a distillery in southern Finland, 45 km from Helsinki, where the bottled mixture of ethanol, tar and gasoline was bundled with matches. The production totalled 450,000 Molotov Cocktails throughout the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true,"cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","i